---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Paseo de la Castellana | Carlos Menco Guardo" mainClass="main-content main-content--project-detail" activePage="demo-castellana" pageScripts={["/js/project-scroll-gradient.js"]}>
  <div class="content--sidebar">
    <div class="project-header">
      <div class="project-img-wrapper">
        <img src="/imgs/demo-castellana-preview.svg" alt="Paseo de la Castellana redesign demo preview" />
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="s1">
      <span class="project-detail-year">2026</span>
      <h5 class="project-detail-title">Paseo de la Castellana Demo</h5>
      <p class="project-detail-description">A redesign proposal for a shopping center experience, currently built in HTML as a demo and planned as a future WordPress implementation.</p>
      <a href="https://demo-castellana.carlosmenco.site/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noreferrer noopener" class="external-link">View demo <span class="external-link-icon"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M4.22876 4.22924V5.5586L9.49435 5.56332L3.75736 11.3003L4.70017 12.2431L10.4372 6.50613L10.4324 11.7717H11.7712V4.22924H4.22876Z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg></span></a>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Overview</h6>
      <p>Paseo de la Castellana is a redesign demo for a shopping center website. The concept presents the mall as a complete destination for food, shopping, entertainment, cinema, events, and visitor information.</p>
      <p>The current version is HTML-first, useful for validating the creative direction and content structure before moving into a more editable WordPress implementation.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Role</h6>
      <p>Redesign proposal, HTML implementation, content structure, user journey planning, responsive layout, and WordPress migration planning.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Challenge</h6>
      <p>A shopping center site needs to support several visitor intents at the same time: finding stores, checking events, discovering restaurants, planning a visit, and understanding what makes the place worth visiting.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Solution</h6>
      <ul>
        <li>Created a demo experience around directory discovery, events, restaurants, entertainment, and visitor actions.</li>
        <li>Used HTML to move quickly and validate the structure before committing to a CMS build.</li>
        <li>Planned the content so it can later become WordPress-managed sections, listings, events, and landing pages.</li>
        <li>Focused the narrative on the shopping center as a place to eat, play, enjoy, and return.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="s1">
      <h6>Outcome</h6>
      <p>The demo gives the project a strong visual and structural starting point for a future WordPress site, with clearer paths for visitors and a more modern destination-style presentation.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
